report={'review':'Independent Validator Mode A contract129 attempt1; static only','feature':'129','contract_id':'129','reviewer':'/root/validator133','revision_reviewed':0,'root_release':'a6ddbee2cef7097b1b6747017d987b4f1aec24e7','reviewed_commit':proposal,'proposal_sha256':sha(raw),'workspace':'/home/cnross/.tmp/nizam-133-bundle-validator1','branch':'review/129-mode-a1','issues':[{'verification_index':'all seven new SBCL acceptance leaves; test_obligations.freeze and gate_sequence[1]','criterion':'The mandated independently frozen intended red must be feasible on the named pre-repair product and distinct from setup/CLI/missing-capability failure.','severity':'high','evidence':'Parent runtime_session.validate_request(open-session) permits only expected_generation/expected_lease_epoch as optional fields, operation_data parses every expression as stub JSON, and Supervisor.prepare launches fixed fixtures/runtime_session/stub_runtime.py. No tools/sbcl_session_loop.lisp or SBCL selection/backend exists. Contract nevertheless requires real SBCL correlated dispatch/progress and an intended semantic red on unmodified product before any product repair, while excluding missing source/selectors/SBCL/CLI/setup from that red. New runner flags alone cannot create the absent product execution path.','required_fix':'Propose a coherent, explicitly staged pre-repair deficiency/red admission and implementation sequence for the absent backend. State exact baseline capability/classification and positive controls, retain independent frozen tests/review and actual exits/revisions, and avoid presenting unsupported-selector/setup failure as a deeper SBCL semantic regression. Any authorized preparatory Source checkpoint or amended red classification must be explicit and independently re-reviewed before code. Validator supplies no implementation or bypass.'}],'missing_acceptance_coverage':[],'unsupported_claims':[],'confirmed':['Seven new verification commands match the entire129 acceptance array exactly, followed by inherited core-ready and both compliance modes. Feature scope remains the two product files and independently owned runner expansion;130hermetic ASDF/131CI-fullmatrix/132readiness and schema/stub-fixture/installed changes are excluded.','Separate Generator/test-author/bundle-reviewer/Validator/freshQA roles, immutable bundle/source, ModeB, exactlyone extra, Root evidence and lifecycle ownership are explicit. Activation/numeric allocation and105normalmerge precede Source;105mainallfive precedes newintegration. Proposal currently grants preparation only.','Required condition-before-unwind, bounded hostile reporting, partial-load inconsistency/quarantine, correlated cleanup cancellation, owned-group observed termination, wait/reattach continuity and original stub regression are mapped to verification obligations. Proposed statuses/condition references fit existing closed operation schema; runtime selection is specifically assigned to private controller metadata, not an invented session-record field.','Existing expression record is a string and can carry Lisp after runtime-aware admission changes, but current product only implements stub parsing. This confirms the red-order conflict rather than a runtime result. Requested diagnostic depth/length/time/bytes must stay within existing public record interfaces or receive an explicit reviewed change; no schema expansion is authorized.','Proposed2100 including650product/450tests/1000process and phase7350/9555/process3750 remain unallocated; carried preparation counts once, prior133failed3024/2600 exception is not transferable. No contract repair, Source/test/runtime probe/model/install/CI/measurement or Rootstate edit by Validator.'],'evidence':{'static_frame':'/home/cnross/.tmp/nizam-129-mode-a1/review.execution.json','static_stdout':'/home/cnross/.tmp/nizam-129-mode-a1/review.stdout.txt','controller_sha256':sha(source),'runner_sha256':sha((root/'tools/test_runtime_session.py').read_bytes()),'root_counter_attempt':1,'diff_check_pid':p.pid,'diff_check_actual_exit':p.returncode},'final_verdict':{'approved':False,'summary':'Reject the contradictory intended-semantic-red ordering for a wholly absent SBCL backend; bounded scope and verification mapping otherwise remain supported.'}}
